  "gandhinagar": [
    "Gandhinagar weddings booked from our Ahmedabad base are usually planned as a single travelling assignment rather than a standard local visit, so venue and season details matter more than they would for an in-town booking. Resort and destination-style venues around Gandhinagar often have their own preparation spaces, which we confirm with the property directly where possible, and lawn or outdoor venues need a weather-aware backup plan for the styling area. Peak wedding season brings more competing bookings across the wider Ahmedabad region, so Gandhinagar dates during busy weeks should be confirmed with more lead time than an off-season date would need. Because the team is travelling specifically for the Gandhinagar booking, we also factor in road or transfer time when planning the arrival buffer — an earlier ceremony time generally means an earlier departure from Ahmedabad. If the venue is unfamiliar to us, sharing photos or a location pin in advance helps us plan the right team size and equipment before the day itself, rather than adjusting on arrival.",
    "Choosing a package for an Gandhinagar wedding starts with the same questions as any booking — how many people, what level of detail for the groom, and whether the wider baraat needs full styling or a simpler coordinated look — but travel from Ahmedabad adds planning time worth building in. Because the team commits to a specific date and route for a Gandhinagar assignment, package and quantity decisions are best finalised a week or two earlier than they would be for a local wedding, giving enough time to prepare fabric and confirm the final artist count. If your Gandhinagar celebration includes multiple functions across a short trip, a combined package covering all of them is usually more practical than booking each date separately. We're glad to talk through a realistic package once we know your approximate headcount, the venue type, and whether the wedding is a single day or a multi-day stay — share what you have so far and we'll take it from there.",
  ],
  "sanand": [
    "Sanand weddings booked from our Ahmedabad base are usually planned as a single travelling assignment rather than a standard local visit, so venue and season details matter more than they would for an in-town booking. Resort and destination-style venues around Sanand often have their own preparation spaces, which we confirm with the property directly where possible, and lawn or outdoor venues need a weather-aware backup plan for the styling area. Peak wedding season brings more competing bookings across the wider Ahmedabad region, so Sanand dates during busy weeks should be confirmed with more lead time than an off-season date would need. Because the team is travelling specifically for the Sanand booking, we also factor in road or transfer time when planning the arrival buffer — an earlier ceremony time generally means an earlier departure from Ahmedabad. If the venue is unfamiliar to us, sharing photos or a location pin in advance helps us plan the right team size and equipment before the day itself, rather than adjusting on arrival.",
    "For a travelling Sanand booking, the right package depends on guest count just as it would locally, but travel adds one more variable worth planning around: how many functions the team needs to cover during the trip. A single-ceremony booking is the most straightforward — one date, one venue, one styling window. A multi-function Sanand trip, covering a haldi or sangeet alongside the main wedding, is usually more efficient as one combined package rather than separate bookings, since the team is already travelling from Ahmedabad and can plan artist time across the full stay. Fabric and accessory choices work the same way they would for a local booking — a coordinated palette for the groom and family, reviewed against outfit references before the team departs. Because Sanand bookings involve travel, we recommend finalising the package a little earlier than you might for an in-town wedding, so fabric, artist numbers and the travel schedule can all be confirmed together rather than adjusted at short notice.",
  ],
